  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/machine_pool.py `lease()`: `if LEASE_ENV in environ: parent = _parse_lease(...); yield Lease(nested=True, ...)`. `_open_descriptors` silently skips descriptors that fail `os.fstat`, so a nested process whose inherited fds are gone still yields a pooled nested Lease and acquires nothing.",
      "id": "nested-lease-trusts-env-without-verifying-held-tokens",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "A nested run reuses any DEV_PLATFORM_MACHINE_POOL_LEASE found in the environment without checking that the lease's slot descriptors are still held. A stale or leaked exported lease (for example an environment captured from a finished run, or a child started without pass_fds) makes the run proceed unpooled and silently. The spec says a run SHALL NOT run outside the pool, and nested reuse is only justified because the parent holds the tokens."
    }
